Yes, I agree with Gary.  Whenever you are dropping some controls you are essentially always estimating the ATE.  (That's a bit of an oversimplification but not too far off).

But you could estimate the ATE using subclassification.  (But right, not using the MatchIt-generated weights).   You would estimate the effect separately within each subclass and then weight the subclass-specific effects by the proportion of people in that subclass (in the whole population).  I think my 2010 Statistical Science paper talks more about that.  And I think Zelig could implement that but I'm not sure.

Liz


